        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/cranberry_sauce_with_orange?rev=1259275704&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Cranberry Sauce with Orange

(Bon Appetit, November 1997, pg. 164.)

	*  3/4 cup water
	*  1/2 cup packed golden brown sugar
	*  1 12 ounce package cranberries, about 3 cups
	*  2 teaspoons grated orange peel, or 2/3 teaspoons dried orange peel
1. Stir water and sugar in heavy saucepan over medium heat until sugar dissolves. Bring mixture to a boil.2. Add cranberries and orange peel.3. Reduce heat and simmer till cranberries burst, about 5 minutes. Remove from heat. Mixture will thicken as it co…</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/daddychicken?rev=1205111031&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2008-03-09T21:03:51-05:00</dc:date>
        <title>recipes:daddychicken</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/daddychicken?rev=1205111031&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>*  Preheat oven to 360°F
	*  Obtain 4 whole chicken legs, cut in half
	*  Place legs and thighs in pan, removing excess skin where possible
	*  Drizzle olive oil over chicken
	*  Cover first side of chicken with salt, pepper,  Fines Herbes, and basil (resist all temptation to add additional herbs)
	*  Cover pan with aluminum foil</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/flan?rev=1262359485&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2010-01-01T10:24:45-05:00</dc:date>
        <title>recipes:flan</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/recipes/flan?rev=1262359485&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Flan

Oven 350 degrees


	*  6 eggs
	*  2 cups milk
	*  1 teaspoon vanilla extract
	*  1.5 cups sugar

	*  Caramelize half cup sugar in nonstick skillet, stirring constantly. When melted, pour into the bottom of a Pyrex dish.
		*  Beat 6 eggs, or mix in blender. Add milk, vanilla and 1 cup sugar. Beat thoroughly; pour into dish on top of caramelized sugar.
		*  Place Pyrex dish in a larger dish. Add water to the larger dish to half cover the contents of the Pyrex dish. (“Bano Maria”)
		*  Bake 4…</description>
    </item>
